<p>A reader named Madhu sent me a patch for running <a href="https://github.com/jrm-code-project/llambda">llambda.lisp</a> under linux.  This patch uses mmap to pull the weights into the lisp address space outside the heap.</p>
  
  <p>In addition, he tried to use a hugging face model that needed some default values, so he added them.</p>

<p>He reports that he was able to get the model to do inference on his linux box with about an hour of hacking.  I have incorporated his patches and pushed the update to GitHub.</p>